# Build output, and the packages `zig fetch` drops beside the project when
# it is run from this directory.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/
zig-pkg/

# Agent worktrees. These are full checkouts of this repository; committing one
# would nest the repository inside itself.
.claude/

# macOS.
.DS_Store

# Build artefacts from ad-hoc compiler invocations. These carry absolute paths
# from the machine that produced them, which is not something a public
# repository should hand out — and a mutation script leaves a .bak behind if it
# is interrupted mid-run.
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.bak

# Scratch. A section of a source file lifted out while editing it, a patch
# leftover, an editor's swap file: none of them are the package, and one of them
# was committed into src/ and shipped before this line existed.
# `ci/verify-package.sh` reads THIS file to decide what counts as scratch, so a
# pattern added here is also the gate — a tracked file matching any rule below
# fails the build rather than riding along into a release.
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*~

# The example is a separate build graph with its own cache.
examples/*/.zig-cache/
examples/*/zig-out/
